      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/Arabi,_Louisiana",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The 1834 LeBeau Plantation house later became the LeBeau Club, a gambling hotspot in the early 1900s.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/Arabi,_Louisiana",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Buildings in Arabi showcase Colonial Revival, Bungalow/Craftsman, and eclectic 1920s styles, reflecting early 20th‑century trends.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
